plan v2.0.0: the depth contract, and Day 0 rewritten as a hub plus 17 parts

Amend the plan to v2.0.0 (documentation architecture only - no day, ID, phase,
gate, pin or principle 1-14 changed) and rebuild the repository around it.

Plan:
- Principles 15/16/17: depth over density, a day is a unit of subject not of
  time, assume no prior knowledge and finish at production.
- New Part 11, the depth contract: the folder shape, the <section>.<subtopic>
  numbering rule, the ten required sections of a part document (adding "The
  story" and a mandatory "In production"), the twelve required hub sections,
  the foundation/working/production level ladder, and the seven failure modes
  this replaces.

Tooling:
- scripts/depth_check.py enforces the machine-checkable half of Part 11,
  including a hard failure on any time estimate in a day folder.
- scripts/tracker.py generates docs/TRACKER.md from the curriculum index plus
  what is on disk; CURRICULUM_INDEX.md loses its status column so plan and
  progress cannot drift.
- ./m rewritten as a bash dispatcher with set -euo pipefail, adding depth,
  parts and tracker, and tolerating pytest exit code 5 (no tests collected).
- .claude/skills/{day,done,gate,freshness} rewritten for the new format.
- .gitattributes made authoritative (* text=auto eol=lf), since this machine
  has core.autocrlf=true and ./m must stay LF.

Day 0 - Setup: the toolchain, the skeleton, and the driver:
- 17 part documents across 4 sections: the toolchain that owns the environment,
  the repository built in the right order, the ./m driver, and the three
  machines that make ninety days self-enforcing.
- Each part carries all ten contract sections and ends at production.
- ./m depth 0 passes; ./m check is green.

Migration:
- The entire v1.1.0 repository (91 lessons, old docs, old skills, pre-written
  src/ and tests/, old driver and CI workflow) moved with git mv to legacy/.
  Nothing deleted; history intact. Reference material to mine, never structure
  to copy.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
